      "explanation": "The exponent \\(30\\) is twice \\(15\\), so write \\(15^{30}=(15^2)^{15}\\). This makes the numerator and denominator products of fifteen factors that can be paired:\n\\[\n\\frac{15^{30}}{45^{15}}\n=\\left(\\frac{15^2}{45}\\right)^{15}\n=\\left(\\frac{225}{45}\\right)^{15}\n=\\boxed{5^{15}}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
